WEBVTT

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:05.646
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> <b>Jackson, 17</b>

00:00:08.186 --> 00:00:10.345
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> What kind of phone do you have?

00:00:10.772 --> 00:00:12.182
<v><b>Jackson:</b></v> An iPhone 14.

00:00:12.882 --> 00:00:13.994
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> How old is it?

00:00:14.588 --> 00:00:16.628
<v><b>Jackson:</b></v> I’m not sure how old it is.

00:00:17.012 --> 00:00:20.251
I got it in August, but it was my mom’s old phone.

00:00:21.084 --> 00:00:23.438
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> How often do you change phones?

00:00:24.041 --> 00:00:27.411
<v><b>Jackson:</b></v> Probably every eighteen months to two years.

00:00:28.389 --> 00:00:31.461
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> What do you use your phone for the most?

00:00:31.934 --> 00:00:34.530
<v><b>Jackson:</b></v> Texting friends and social media.

00:00:35.142 --> 00:00:38.010
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> How often do you make actual phone calls?

00:00:38.463 --> 00:00:39.596
<v><b>Jackson:</b></v> Almost never.

00:00:40.603 --> 00:00:42.576
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> What apps do you use a lot?

00:00:43.033 --> 00:00:46.861
<v><b>Jackson:</b></v> I play a lot of sudoku. I have a sudoku app.

00:00:47.542 --> 00:00:50.527
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> Do you have any unusual apps on your phone?

00:00:51.184 --> 00:00:54.556
<v><b>Jackson:</b></v> Not really. I think all my apps are pretty normal.

00:00:58.913 --> 00:01:00.839
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> <b>Sophie, 40</b>

00:01:03.172 --> 00:01:05.260
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> What kind of phone do you have?

00:01:05.803 --> 00:01:07.506
<v><b>Sophie:</b></v> It’s a Samsung phone.

00:01:08.065 --> 00:01:09.019
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> How old is it?

00:01:09.632 --> 00:01:11.732
<v><b>Sophie:</b></v> About a year old, I think.

00:01:12.658 --> 00:01:14.910
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> How often do you change phones?

00:01:15.528 --> 00:01:18.685
<v><b>Sophie:</b></v> I hate changing phones, so not often.

00:01:19.511 --> 00:01:26.276
Unfortunately, my last phone only lasted three years because the battery stopped working.

00:01:27.349 --> 00:01:29.908
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> What do you use your phone for the most?

00:01:30.706 --> 00:01:34.874
<v><b>Sophie:</b></v> I checked this on my phone, and it said mainly Google.

00:01:35.611 --> 00:01:40.674
I research places I'm going to go to, I check my email,

00:01:41.391 --> 00:01:47.834
I plan trips using Google maps, I look for reviews for things I'm thinking of buying,

00:01:48.678 --> 00:01:54.745
l Iook up meanings of words, I use Google Translate. All on Google.

00:01:55.762 --> 00:01:58.928
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> How often do you make actual phone calls?

00:02:00.665 --> 00:02:02.489
<v><b>Sophie:</b></v> Once in a blue moon.

00:02:03.784 --> 00:02:05.530
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> What apps do you use a lot?

00:02:06.264 --> 00:02:11.064
<v><b>Sophie:</b></v> I also checked this, and it said a game called Tile Match!

00:02:11.451 --> 00:02:13.348
I was really surprised!

00:02:14.221 --> 00:02:16.981
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> Do you have any unusual apps on your phone?

00:02:17.591 --> 00:02:21.470
<v><b>Sophie:</b></v> I use an app called FlightTracker to pass the time

00:02:21.471 --> 00:02:25.407
while I’m waiting for a flight or waiting to meet someone.

00:02:26.146 --> 00:02:30.221
You can follow the path of a plane when it’s coming toward the airport.

00:02:31.114 --> 00:02:34.057
I also have an app for jigsaw puzzles.

00:02:34.517 --> 00:02:40.273
It's really relaxing to do jigsaw puzzles on your phone. Who knew!

00:02:44.283 --> 00:02:46.569
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> <b>Rose, 65</b>

00:02:48.872 --> 00:02:51.365
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> What kind of phone do you have?

00:02:51.898 --> 00:02:55.042
<v><b>Rose:</b></v> I think it’s an iPhone 13.

00:02:55.590 --> 00:02:57.205
An iPhone, anyway.

00:02:57.845 --> 00:02:58.907
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> How old is it?

00:02:59.605 --> 00:03:01.878
<v><b>Rose:</b></v> I got it about two years ago.

00:03:02.877 --> 00:03:05.374
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> How often do you change phones?

00:03:05.998 --> 00:03:11.434
<v><b>Rose:</b></v> Every three or four years, usually because the battery isn’t working very well.

00:03:12.217 --> 00:03:15.159
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> What do you use your phone for the most?

00:03:15.705 --> 00:03:19.630
<v><b>Rose:</b></v> Texting people, checking the news and weather,

00:03:20.123 --> 00:03:25.123
sometimes Google Maps for directions, calling taxis,

00:03:25.143 --> 00:03:28.328
taking photos, listening to the radio.

00:03:28.855 --> 00:03:31.663
Oh, and I sometimes play solitaire.

00:03:32.630 --> 00:03:35.760
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> How often do you make actual phone calls?

00:03:36.246 --> 00:03:37.539
<v><b>Rose:</b></v> Very rarely.

00:03:37.979 --> 00:03:43.102
Only to family or friends when I get bored of writing really long messages.

00:03:43.949 --> 00:03:45.942
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> What apps do you use a lot?

00:03:46.554 --> 00:03:50.884
<v><b>Rose:</b></v> WhatsApp, Uber, and other taxi apps I have,

00:03:51.370 --> 00:03:57.538
the camera, BBC News, BBC Sounds (that’s the radio app).

00:03:58.171 --> 00:03:59.577
And banking apps.

00:04:00.424 --> 00:04:03.150
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> Do you have any unusual apps on your phone?

00:04:03.843 --> 00:04:08.761
<v><b>Rose:</b></v> I have an app for identifying birds by recording their songs

00:04:09.081 --> 00:04:12.904
and another to identify flowers by taking a photo.

00:04:13.544 --> 00:04:17.281
I sometimes use them when I go for a walk in the country.